18. Spanning Tree Protocol (STP)

STP stands for:

Spanning Tree Protocol

STP helps prevent Layer 2 switching loops when redundant network paths exist.

Example
Switch A
 ↘   ↖
  Switch B

A Layer 2 loop can cause serious network problems such as broadcast storms.

STP helps manage redundant paths to prevent such loops.

Interview Answer

STP is a protocol used to prevent Layer 2 switching loops in networks with redundant links.

